precision mismatch: expected f32, got f64
Blocker: the f32-only signature on `Nautilus.Special` (draft parked at
docs/issue_drafts/nautilus-special-f32-only.md), with nautilus#56 the sibling
bound and chelis#902 the structural fix. `Nautilus.Special.erf` is f32-only, so
a Shoals f64 grad path cannot call it and `Shoals.Pricing` carries its own
kernel. That kernel now evaluates Cody's rational approximation at a measured
1.9e-16 max absolute error; the duplication is what remains, not the accuracy.

Three upstream repairs bear on this and they are disjoint. An f64 signature on
`Nautilus.Special` removes the reason to duplicate -- that is the one this
probe detects, and it has no issue number yet. nautilus#56 is the f32
original's own A&S bound: fixing it changes those coefficients but not the
signature, so this probe would still fail. chelis#902 would give the language a
canonical `erf` with a stated accuracy and removes both. Not a chelis
arithmetic defect: f64 arithmetic is evaluated correctly.

Do not cite nautilus#12 here. It is the `Nautilus.LinAlg` signature barrier and
says nothing about `Nautilus.Special`; an earlier revision of this sidecar
cited it, which made the de-narrowing branch below unexecutable.

Measured on 0.18.6: this exact probe reports `precision mismatch: expected f32,
got f64`, i.e. the symbol resolves and refuses the width. An earlier draft of
this probe assumed `erf` was absent entirely and expected `unbound variable`;
running it is what corrected that.

On pass: determine which repair landed. If `Nautilus.Special` gained an f64
signature, replace `Shoals.Pricing.erf64`'s body with the package `erf` and
keep the accuracy rows in docs/CHELIS_SURFACE.md, since the coefficients are
unchanged -- unless nautilus#56 landed with it, in which case re-derive them
from the new coefficients' bound. If chelis#902 landed, call the language `erf`
and re-derive those rows from its [05-OP-N] atom's stated bound instead of from
A&S. Either way promote this probe to tests/ and archive the
docs/UPSTREAM_BUGS.md entry in the same change set.
